THE definitive OOM root cause (singleplayer terrain demo 'physics frozen, RAM climbs to ~4GB OOM on world load'), found via a self-contained Playwright heap-capture (scripts/heap-capture.mjs) + per-step [BUILD-HEAP] probes in app.js _buildWorldScenery: the heap exploded inside rocks.update -> streamRing -> _rockSpiralOffsets(span). _rockSpiralOffsets / _vegSpiralOffsets / _spiralOffsets (Rocks.js, Vegetation.js, Grass.js - ALL THREE identical) was a hand-written outward spiral that NEVER TERMINATED: the inner `if (Math.hypot(x,z) > span) break` only exits the for-loop, but the outer `while (Math.abs(x) <= span || Math.abs(z) <= span)` stays true forever (one axis is always within span as the walk oscillates past the corner), so it `out.push([x,z])` until the JS heap hit ~4GB and OOM'd, freezing the worker tick. REPRODUCED EXACTLY: a node one-liner of _rockSpiralOffsets(12) OOM'd at 3980MB. FIX (commit c4633cc8): replace all three with a direct nearest-first grid - `for dz/-span..span for dx/-span..span if hypot(dx,dz)<=span out.push; out.sort(by dist)` - bounded (~pi*span^2, span=12 -> 441 offsets) and terminating. VERIFIED: full demo (planet+rocks+grass+veg) now builds to ~203MB heap (was 4GB OOM); rocks-only 90MB. KEY LESSONS: (1) ALL my earlier 'fixes' were WRONG/secondary - texture-size cuts, snapshot postMessage coalescing, broken-veg-shader gate, d3-octree NaN+quantize guard (d3-octree was a red herring - tested non-degenerate; the worker octree 40% CPU in the profile was the worker tick, a SEPARATE cost from the main-thread 4GB). (2) BAD ASSUMPTION I made for a LONG time: that the dev iGPU 'couldn't render the planet' and blocked - WRONG, it is the SAME GPU as the user's; the 'GPU build block' WAS this OOM infinite-loop all along. Once I stopped assuming GPU and actually captured the heap, the bug fell out in minutes. (3) When JS heap->OOM with FLAT DOM nodes, it's a pure JS alloc - a node repro of the suspect function + a Playwright heap-capture that survives the crash (own chromium, long timeout, console listener) beats the plugkit browser verb's 14s cap. Supersedes the earlier OOM memos [[d3-octree-spatialindex-4gb-oom-nan-coincident]] [[singleplayer-snapshot-postmessage-oom-leak]] [[gpu-program-leak-broken-veg-on-planet-fallback]] - those were real-but-secondary; THIS spiral was the OOM.